## PART 0 — BEFORE YOU OPEN STITCH

### What is Google Stitch?
<https://stitch.withgoogle.com> — Google Labs' AI-powered UI design tool. You type a detailed prompt → it generates a high-fidelity UI design + frontend code scaffold. Powered by Gemini 2.5 Pro (Pro mode) and Gemini 2.5 Flash (Standard mode).

### Generation Limits (as of 2026)
| Mode | Model | Monthly Limit | When to Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Standard** | Gemini 2.5 Flash | ~350 generations | Quick iterations, minor edits, variants |
| **Pro / Experimental** | Gemini 2.5 Pro | ~200 generations | Your primary screens — use this for everything important |

**Rule:** Always use **Pro mode** for the first generation of any important screen. Switch to Standard only for quick variants or small tweaks.

### What Stitch Outputs
1. A visual UI mockup (rendered on canvas)
2. Frontend code (HTML/CSS or component scaffold)
3. A `DESIGN.md` file (your design system rules)
4. Figma paste (copy directly into Figma)

### Export Workflow After Stitch
```
Stitch Design → Export DESIGN.md → Paste to Figma → Reference while implementing in Next.js/Tailwind
```

