## PART 4 — DESIGN.MD EXPORT + FIGMA WORKFLOW

### Step 4.1 — Export DESIGN.md

After your design system screen (Screen 0 from Part 1) is generated:

1. In Stitch canvas, click the **"..."** menu (top right of canvas)
2. Click **"Export DESIGN.md"**
3. Save the file as `DESIGN.md` in your project root
4. **Paste this DESIGN.md content** at the top of every subsequent Stitch prompt under a `[DESIGN SYSTEM]` section — this ensures visual consistency across all screens

### Step 4.2 — Paste to Figma (After Each Screen)

After each screen is generated and you're happy with it:
1. Click **"Paste to Figma"** button in Stitch
2. In Figma: `Ctrl+V` (or `Cmd+V`) — the design pastes as native Figma layers
3. Organize Figma pages: one page per screen (Page: Dashboard, Page: Collections, etc.)
4. Apply **Auto Layout** to all pasted frames for responsive prep
5. Create a **Component Library page** in Figma with all cards, buttons, badges extracted from your screens

### Step 4.3 — Prototype Linking in Stitch

After generating all screens, use Stitch's **Prototype mode**:
1. Click **"Prototype"** tab in Stitch
2. Link: Sidebar "Dashboard" → Dashboard screen
3. Link: "Collections" nav → Collections page
4. Link: Collection card click → Collection Detail
5. Link: Video card click → Watch Page
6. Link: "Share" button → Share modal
7. Click **"Play"** to preview the full interactive flow

